{{also|Baħamas|Bahama's}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|The Bahamas}}

===Etymology===
Disputed; probably from {{der|en|es|[[baja]] [[mar]]||shallow sea}} or {{der|en|tnq|ba ha ma||big upper middle land}}, via Spanish.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|bə-hä'-məz|a=UK,US}}, {{IPA|en|/bəˈhɑː.məz/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Bahamas.ogg|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=the Bahamas}}

# {{senseid|en|Q778}}{{place|en|archipelago/and/country|r/Caribbean|official=[[Commonwealth of The Bahamas]]}}.

====Usage notes====
* Like other country names, ''The Bahamas'' is usually construed as a singular noun:
*:{{good||The Bahamas is a nice place to live.}}
*:{{bad||The Bahamas are a horrible place to live.}}
*But because [[Bahama]] refers to an individual island, one can still describe the islands using ''Bahamas'' as a plural:
*:{{good||Many species of crab live on the Bahamas.}}

